⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Ta-Kumsaw
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Ta-Kumsaw:C1:c29caa⟧

WHO   — Ta-Kumsaw — the war chief who hears the green music
WHAT  — The warrior of Red Prophet — the proud, doomed leader of the Red resistance, brother to the peace-choosing Prophet, who carries the boy Alvin through the living land and is broken at last by the treachery of those who will not stop coming.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the land is one living body and the White man's plow and axe are a wound; because a people in tune with the green music cannot share the world with a people who hear nothing; because if the land must die he will die fighting for it rather than live to watch it killed.
HOW   — By the greensong that carries a runner tirelessly through forest no White foot can cross, by the land-sense that knows every deer and bird and root, by war and oratory and the binding of scattered tribes into one fist — and by refusing, where his brother chooses peace, to lay down the tomahawk.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  The land is one body and I am its tomahawk hand — while one tree of the old forest still stands, the green music has a war chief.

spoken token : thul-laem-kys   ·   hex : c29caa
